+````markdown name=docs/runbooks/auto_promotion_runbook.md
+# Auto-Promotion Runbook (Operator-facing)
+
+Purpose
+- Describe the safe auto-promotion flow for low-risk changes and the safeguards for high-risk changes.
+
+Pre-requisites
+- Policy engine reachable at POLICY_ENGINE_URL and seeded with the delegation_matrix/auto_policy_catalog.yaml
+- COSIGN_KEY_REF and EVIDENCE_BUCKET configured
+- GitHub repo configured with the auto-merge GH Action (.github/workflows/auto_merge_policy.yml)
+- Vault path for signoffs (optional)
+
+Flow (high-level)
+1. Developer creates PR (Advisor agent may create generated PR)
+2. PR Action runs:
+   - Policy engine evaluated; if "auto" approval and role checks pass, the action will merge the PR automatically.
+   - Otherwise, PR is labeled `requires-approval` and human reviewer must approve/merge.
+3. On merge for a canary-enabled deployment:
+   - Canary controller applies canary (GitOps or manifest update).
+   - Acceptance tests run (automated). If pass, promotion occurs per policy.
+   - If canary fails, automatic rollback is created and attestation evidence is generated and uploaded.
+4. Legal signoff:
+   - If the policy requires legal_signoff, the auto_signoff_controller or webhook_receiver is used to create a ticket for legal.
+   - Legal must record signoff (close/COMMENT with "SIGNED") or post to LEGAL_WEBHOOK. On signoff, Aegis will cosign a signoff manifest and upload to evidence bucket.
+
+Operator checks before enabling auto-mode
+- Confirm policy rules are conservative: only low-risk actions set to "auto".
+- Run 100 dry-run promotions in staging and confirm rollback and attestation behaviors.
+- Ensure WORM bucket and cosign signing verify cleanly (cosign verify).
+- Confirm that vault kill-switch is set and tested.
+
+Emergency (kill-switch)
+- To disable all automation: vault kv put secret/aegis/kill_switch value=on
+- Verify automation aborts by attempting a known low-risk auto flow and ensuring it stops.
+
+Audit
+- Attestation bundles, signoff manifests and evidence uploads must be verifiable via cosign and stored in WORM bucket.
+- Use ops/attestation/reproducibility_check.sh to validate rebuilds and store results.
+````
